{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. Obs are done already. Temperature is thirty seven point eight, pulse ninety six, sats 97 percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thanks sister. Umm, file says sickle cell disease, this is Thabo, twenty two. What brought you today?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Pain.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pain, ja. My mind goes straight to the bones with sickle cell. Where is it?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Legs.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Only the legs, or...",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Back.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Legs and the back. How long now?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): Two days.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Two days. Is it deep in the bone, or more...",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Deep.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Deep, right. How bad is it, can you walk or is it really sore?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): Bad.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): So I've got deep bone pain in the legs and the back for two days, and it's bad. Correct?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (NURSE): He walked from the taxi rank. Blood pressure one eighteen over seventy two, breathing eighteen.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): One eighteen over seventy two and a rate of eighteen, that's fine. Any fever with this?",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): A bit.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): A bit, and thirty seven point eight is only a mild fever. Err, have you been coughing?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): No cough. Are you short of breath?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): No shortness of breath. When did the fever start?",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry, jumping in, the scale is broken so we never got a weight.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ag, you don't know, so we can't date the fever. Have you lost any weight?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Maybe.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Maybe, that's too vague, I'm not writing weight loss down. What medicines are you taking?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Folic acid.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Folic acid. What dose?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): Five.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Five milligram, once a day, by mouth?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): And hydroxurea, are you still on that?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is it five hundred milligram, or...",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (PATIENT): Five hundred.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): Five hundred milligram every day?",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Let me feel. Shins are a bit tender, there's no swelling, calves are soft. Back muscles are not in spasm, so this is the bone.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm thinking a mild vaso-occlusive episode. Bone pain for two days, low grade fever, nothing in the chest history. That's a working impression, not a final diagnosis.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): We'll do bloods today, a full blood count, a retic count, and urea and electrolytes. Sister, can you take them?",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (NURSE): Ja, I'll draw them before he leaves. Lab is still open.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): For the pain I'll start paracetamol, one gram by mouth, four times a day. Drink about three litres of water today as well, not cooldrink.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (DOCTOR): Keep going with the folic acid and the hydroxurea, don't stop them. If the pain gets worse tonight or you become short of breath, come back to emergency straight away.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (DOCTOR): Otherwise you are booked to see me in two days, Thursday, so we can go through the results. That's set, not only if you feel bad.",
  "[SEG0048] person_3 (PATIENT): Thursday."
 ],
